  "2026-10-29T09:30:34.908Z",codex-agent,"UPSTREAM CANDIDATE\n\nStandalone reproduction against an isolated installed @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28 SDK, with no tracker or git dependency. In a scratch npm project: npm install --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.28 @toon-format/toon@4.4.0 (public registry configuration only); save as repro.mjs and run node repro.mjs. No package pin was changed.\n\nExact script:\n```js\nimport { encode } from \"@toon-format/toon\";\nimport { encodeToon } from \"@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/testing\";\nimport { createRequire } from \"node:module\";\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconsole.log({ node: process.version, pm: require(\"@unbrained/pm-cli/package.json\").version,\n  toon: require(\"./node_modules/@toon-format/toon/package.json\").version,\n  pmToon: require(\"./node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/package.json\").version });\nfor (const [name, render] of [[\"encoder\", encode], [\"SDK encodeToon\", encodeToon]]) {\n  try { render({ assumption: \"\\ud800\" }); }\n  catch (error) { console.log(name + \"\\n\" + error.stack.replaceAll(process.cwd(), \"<scratch>\")); }\n}\n```\n\nVersions and complete stacks (only the scratch-directory prefix is replaced):\n```text\n{ node: 'v24.19.0', pm: '2026.10.28', toon: '4.4.0', pmToon: '4.4.0' }\nencoder\nTypeError: Cannot encode string value containing an unpaired surrogate U+D800 at index 0\n    at assertNoLoneSurrogate (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1291:9)\n    at normalizeValue (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1253:3)\n    at normalizeValue (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1274:39)\n    at encodeLines (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1733:26)\n    at encode (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1690:20)\n    at file://<scratch>/repro.mjs:9:9\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:439:25)\n    at async node:internal/modules/esm/loader:643:26\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:101:5)\nSDK encodeToon\nTypeError: Cannot encode string value containing an unpaired surrogate U+D800 at index 0\n    at assertNoLoneSurrogate (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1291:9)\n    at normalizeValue (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1253:3)\n    at normalizeValue (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1274:39)\n    at encodeLines (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1733:26)\n    at encode (file://<scratch>/node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/node_modules/@toon-format/toon/dist/index.mjs:1690:20)\n    at file://<scratch>/repro.mjs:9:9\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:439:25)\n    at async node:internal/modules/esm/loader:643:26\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:101:5)\n```\n\nOrigin: @toon-format/toon assertNoLoneSurrogate via normalizeValue, not pm-changelog code. Both the direct encoder and the supported SDK testing encodeToon path reject the lone code unit. Encoder rejection of ill-formed Unicode may be intentional; the package must prepare or refuse text before encoding, and this candidate does not claim an encoder bug for valid Unicode. The orchestrator can assess whether the host needs a typed boundary refusal. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-29T09:57:25.730Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 class audit: all six direct TOON encoder sites now share one Unicode-safe wire boundary, as do standalone JSON, scoped host JSON, export JSON, audit TOON cells and error envelopes. Contract assumptions/commands/evidence, audience notes/resolutions, upgrade titles/bodies and native ID attribution normalize before producer comparisons; valid Unicode and whitespace are exact. The standard node:util toUSVString replaces each lone surrogate with U+FFFD (also verified in Bun). No private SDK import was added: the installed SDK exposes native write validation, not a public leaf-replacement primitive. Internal snapshots, signatures, revision/idempotency digests and durable serialization remain untouched. Dynamic key collisions refuse with typed invalid_unicode_output and field object key instead of losing data. Signed correction records keep their prior strict validator. The property corpus also exposed package-local audit header/cell escaping of controls; official TOON escaping now preserves those values without changing normal output. No existing test was weakened."
  "2026-10-29T09:57:27.408Z",codex-agent,"UPSTREAM CANDIDATE addendum: the pinned 2026.10.26 SDK already refuses native persisted lone surrogates with code text_unpaired_surrogate, field change_facets[0].text, before writing any item. The candidate is therefore not a claim that native write validation is missing. The package failure was reachable through its public pure SDK builders/formatters accepting arbitrary JavaScript text. The non-git integration test retains the SDK refusal, then persists the package-normalized producer output and compares complete state read back through the SDK before/after all host and standalone JSON/TOON commands. The standalone 2026.10.28 SDK codec reproduction and complete encoder-origin stacks remain in the earlier UPSTREAM CANDIDATE comment."
  "2026-10-29T10:11:31.630Z",codex-agent,"Additional producer audit: every arbitrary text slice and URI encoder was checked. Body previews and fallback date labels could split a valid emoji pair; they now truncate whole Unicode characters. Item-link URI components now pass through the same Unicode policy before encodeURIComponent, preventing an untyped URIError. Other slices use array counts or ASCII delimiters and cannot split a valid pair. The expanded 500-string corpus now covers 45500 report-field cases (both encodings), generated documents/summary/selection, dynamic keys, source resolutions, SDK-produced IDs, host markers, siblings, control characters, UTF-8 oracle comparisons and the actual non-git native guard/read-back path. The new output module measured 100% L/B/F. No extra SDK state normalization, snapshot/digest rewrite, or test weakening was introduced."
  "2026-10-29T10:31:13.361Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 verification: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 model-based|500 seeded SDK-read\" test/agent-contract-drift.test.ts test/audience-contracts.test.ts test/consumer-upgrades.test.ts test/claim-audit.test.ts passed 32/32. The Unicode file passed 3/3 both directly and through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 240 (seed 0x298f16, 500 strings, 45500 report-field cases, both encodings, independent UTF-8 oracle, SDK native refusal/read-back, twelve real CLI reads without git). Eleven focused transport/correction/export cases and ten preview/date/link cases passed, for 56 focused cases total. Exact additional commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"strict producer|maximum valid Unicode|pure boundaries|standalone and host commands|registered correction handlers|rendered result|result mode|exporter exercises|in-process main|body-preview\" test/release-corrections.test.ts test/extension.test.ts test/cli-coverage.test.ts; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"body-preview|formatDate|formatLocalTimestampDate|format.*date|path segment|parentheses|item references|Unicode\" test/enhancements.test.ts test/generator-coverage.test.ts test/release-context-coverage.test.ts. Typecheck, build, test typecheck and docstring lint passed (38 files, 255 declarations). Package allowlist/content scans: 107 files, zero failures. The copied packed-SDK probe passed its 14 encoding comparisons against the built module; the actual 444-check archive/install matrix remains for CI. Existing long native-state models and every older regression are retained for CI."
  "2026-10-29T10:31:14.795Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: 23 cases and 46 fixed/restored controls are proven in disposable copies this round. The default node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts run proved 20 cases, then its mutation precondition correctly rejected the new date test targeting the public wrapper instead of the changed private formatDate function (not a production/test failure and not reported as a green default run). Corrected that exact target and the function-name matcher; completed node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts \"Unicode-safe fallback date truncation\" \"Unicode-safe link encoding\" (2 cases) and node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts \"parser help agreement\" (1 case). Exact-rule arguments are local resource controls, unknown rules refuse, and CI invokes the unchanged default all-cases mode. Added reverts cover the shared Unicode primitive/wire policy, declaration/audience/upgrade producers, audit TOON escaping, host marker JSON, preview/date truncation and URI encoding. Every mutated behavior failed an assertion and every fixed/restored control passed. All mutations restore in finally and never touch the active checkout; no retained Git history dependency and no existing test weakening."
  "2026-10-29T10:41:05.503Z",codex-agent,"Final normalization consistency check: captured statusSelection Map keys and omittedNonChangeIds Set keys now normalize through the same Unicode boundary as item IDs. Otherwise a malformed caller-supplied ID could lose its frozen done-role meaning after replacement. The 500-string corpus now also checks captured true/false decisions through drift, audience and upgrade builders for every generated ID, and the two focused Unicode boundary tests passed after this adjustment. Production status meaning still comes from the SDK registry/captured policy, never name comparisons. The shared Unicode module remains 100% L/B/F; module-wide feature coverage is reserved for the full gate. No persistent state or digest was changed."
  "2026-10-29T10:48:37.178Z",codex-agent,"Captured-role follow-up proof passed: node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts \"Unicode captured drift status identity\" \"Unicode captured audience status identity\" independently reverts each ID-to-status Map normalization; each mutation fails the 500-string property and each fixed/restored control passes. This raises the proven total to 25 behavioral cases and 50 controls across the documented runs. The latest property also contrasts captured false with a currently done label and captured true with a currently active label, proving both directions retain frozen meaning through drift/audience/upgrades. It passed after this stronger assertion (45500 text-field cases unchanged). Final typechecks, docstring lint and both 107-file package scans pass after the consistency fix. Default CI will execute every revert case without local rule filters."
  "2026-10-29T10:55:41.105Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 gate handoff: product commit bebe9aa is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40860995361; fresh full npm/Bun gates are 0/4 completed and the expanded 444-check packed/default-25-revert results remain pending. Local evidence: 56 focused cases, 500 strings/45500 text-field cases, Unicode helper 100% L/B/F, 25 individually proven reverts/50 controls, 14 built-module SDK encoding probes, and both 107-file package scans passed. UPSTREAM CANDIDATE comments contain the exact standalone 2026.10.28 SDK/encoder reproduction, versions and sanitized complete stacks, plus confirmation that native SDK writes already refuse malformed text. A tracker-only checkpoint follows so final tracker writes precede exact-head CI verification; PR/final report will link that fresh run. The original cutoff is 11:22 UTC and will not reset. Prior 1bf33f7 CI 40844098689 has now passed all four full gates with 960/960 tests each and 100% measured L/B/F; these are prior-head results only. Own claim is released and item remains in progress. Remaining limits: pending fresh full gates and the documented non-atomic SDK read/settings window. Read-only public validation will repeat in CI; latest confirmed baseline remains 206 items, zero declared facets, 422 files unchanged, JSON 144 bytes, TOON 129 bytes and 35931 note bytes."
  "2026-10-29T11:38:51.743Z",codex-agent,"Round 5: origin/main is already an ancestor (13 ahead, 0 behind), worktree clean. General rule: replay validation and omission provenance must be identical before and after the interval boundary; a baseline fold must not discard invalid history. Auditing every tombstone/state-fold path and adding an independent seeded history model, both encodings, non-git SDK/CLI and packed-consumer regressions. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied."
  "2026-10-29T11:43:05.839Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: the package has one declared-obligation tombstone consumer, buildAgentContractDrift; both its baseline and interval passes now call one apply validator before changing active state. Audience contracts publish release-local facets and consumer upgrades replay action prerequisites, neither interprets obligation removals; correction history has its separate existing revision validation. SDK readAgentContractDrift, host and standalone commands, JSON and TOON all delegate to this builder. Pre-from and repeated removals retain every contributor coordinate, omissions survive later valid reintroduction, known births/retirements stay complete, and future releases stay excluded. Seed 0x298ba5e passed 500 histories / 1500 cut reports against an independent state model for baseline, transitions, unchanged references and omissions in both encodings. Added native SDK read-back plus eight no-git CLI reads, and 44 additional packed checks (four archive-SDK encodings, 40 launcher/read-back checks); expected total is now 488, retaining all earlier 444."
  "2026-10-29T11:51:05.628Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 focused validation passed: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 model-based|500 seeded SDK-read\" --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=src/agent-contract-drift.ts test/agent-contract-drift.test.ts test/contract-report-closure.test.ts: 20/20, no failures/skips, 100% drift lines/functions and 98.96% branches. The focused Unicode follow-up node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 model-based|500 seeded SDK-read|real host, standalone\" --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=src/agent-contract-drift.ts test/agent-contract-drift.test.ts test/unicode-contract-output.test.ts passed 10/10 and reached 100% drift branches (its intentionally narrower scope omits the source SDK reader). No thresholds changed. npm run build, npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring passed (38 files, 255 declarations). npm run pack:dry-run and npm run pack:scan each passed 107 files / zero failures. The extracted built-SDK probe passed 18 comparisons; this does not certify archive installations."
  "2026-10-29T11:51:25.046Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 function-only behavioral revert proof: node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts \"baseline replay validates every removal\" \"interval replay validates every removal\" \"orphan provenance\" passed all three cases. In disposable copies, replacing only the baseline validator call with the old unconditional state fold fails the new orphan/model assertions; bypassing the same guard only in the interval pass also fails; retaining only the first orphan contributor fails the existing provenance assertion. Each mutation has a passing fixed control, assertion failure on revert, finally restoration, and passing restored control: three failed mutants / six passing controls. The source worktree was never mutated by the proof. All prior tests and verifier cases remain; default CI now runs 27 cases including the two new replay guards."
  "2026-10-29T11:52:26.069Z",codex-agent,"Pinned PM receipt: PM_AUTHOR=codex-agent node_modules/.bin/pm test pmc-agent-contract-drift --run --only-last --progress --timeout 240 passed the linked baseline-replay command, 3/3 tests, zero failures/skips/timeouts. It includes 500 histories / 1500 cuts and eight actual non-git host/standalone JSON/TOON reads, each followed by native SDK state read-back. Project policy disables automatic result tracking; this comment preserves the receipt without changing that policy. Existing file/doc links cover every changed implementation, regression, verifier, packed acceptance script, README and drift documentation. Tracker remains in progress."
